  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1147 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nShower and storm coverage will likely increase somewhat during \nthe evening and expand south and east as the front likewise pushes\nslowly south and east. The severe weather threat will likely\ndiminish by late evening and overnight as instability wanes, but\nlocally heavy rainfall may occur. Shower and storm chances linger\nthrough Monday from southeast Oklahoma into northwest Arkansas\nbefore the cold front finally clears the area. Much cooler weather\nwill then prevail for much of the next week, with temperatures\nnear the seasonal averages. Low shower and storm chances may\nreturn to parts of northeast Oklahoma late in the week as an upper\nlevel storm system passes to the north of the area.",
